Splits the web GUI login into two screens for users of the
"Local + Timebased One Time Password" (or "LDAP + Timebased One
Time Password") authentication server: username and password first,
the authentication code on a second screen.

The change is purely client-side. The script joins the code and the
password in the order the configured TOTP server expects and submits
the stock login form, so the server-side authentication flow and the
security properties of the combined field are unchanged. Without a
TOTP server selected for the web GUI the login page stays stock.

WWW: https://github.com/akaengineering/opnsense-login-twostep
